{"title":"WBJEE","category":"Engineering","bank":"wbjee","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Biomolecules","count":13,"questions":[{"id":117946,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Biomolecules","exam":"Engineering","examName":"WBJEE","q":"Which of the following statement(s) is/are correct?","options":["Strach is composed of repeating $\\alpha$–D glucose units","Nylon-6 is an addition polymer whereas nylon–6,6 is a condensation polymer","Isoprene is the monomer unit of natural rubber","Bakelite is obtained from reaction between phenol and acetaldehyde"],"answer":2,"solution":"Starch is a polysaccharide composed of repeating $\\alpha$-D-glucose units, which form amylose and amylopectin. Thus, statement (A) is correct.<br><br>Nylon-6 is synthesized from caprolactam and Nylon-6,6 is synthesized from hexamethylenediamine and adipic acid. Both are polyamides and are classified as condensation polymers. Thus, statement (B) is incorrect.<br><br>Natural rubber is a linear polymer of isoprene (2-methyl-1,3-butadiene) and is also called cis-1,4-polyisoprene. Thus, statement (C) is correct.<br><br>Bakelite is a condensation polymer obtained from the reaction between phenol and formaldehyde, not acetaldehyde. Thus, statement (D) is incorrect.<br><br>Answer: Strach is composed of repeating $\\alpha$–D glucose units; Isoprene is the monomer unit of natural rubber","difficulty":"Medium","source":"WBJEE 2026","_marksId":"6a22cafb9b544592bfdee6c8"},{"id":117947,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Biomolecules","exam":"Engineering","examName":"WBJEE","q":"Which of the following statement(s) is/are correct about the given compound?<br><img style=\"width: 200px\" src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fdiagrams%2Fqx-self-b0f0892c1a828da5.png?alt=media&v=stem2\" / data-qx-orig-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-self-b0f0892c1a828da5.png\" data-qx-storage-src=\"/assets/diagrams/qx-self-b0f0892c1a828da5.png\">\n<img style=\"width: 200px\" src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fquizrr%2Fquestion-assets%2Fwbjee%2F2026%2Fwatermarked_images%2Fwbjee_2026__q80_d1.png?alt=media\" />","options":["It exhibits ring-chain tautomerism","It forms osazone with phenylthydrazine","It gives eight (8) stereoisomers","It responds to Tollen's reagent"],"answer":3,"solution":"The given compound is D-glucose, which is an aldohexose.<br><br>(A) D-glucose exhibits ring-chain tautomerism as it exists in an equilibrium between its open-chain aldehyde form and its cyclic hemiacetal forms ($\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ pyranose forms). Thus, this statement is correct.<br><br>(B) D-glucose reacts with three equivalents of phenylhydrazine to form glucosazone (an osazone). Thus, this statement is correct.<br><br>(C) The open-chain form of D-glucose has $4$ chiral centers. The total number of stereoisomers for this constitution is $2^4 = 16$, not $8$. Thus, this statement is incorrect.<br><br>(D) Being an aldose, it is a reducing sugar. The aldehyde group can be oxidized by Tollen's reagent, giving a positive test (silver mirror). Thus, this statement is correct.<br><br>Answer: It exhibits ring-chain tautomerism; It forms osazone with phenylthydrazine; It responds to Tollen's reagent","difficulty":"Medium","source":"WBJEE 2026","_marksId":"6a22cafb9b544592bfdee6c9"},{"id":117948,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Biomolecules","exam":"Engineering","examName":"WBJEE","q":"1.<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fwbjee%252FZYDtnMm7KkZRGUmsS3RyASs50NmcBatE2j8LEOk4Ds0.original.fullsize.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fwbjee%2FZYDtnMm7KkZRGUmsS3RyASs50NmcBatE2j8LEOk4Ds0.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-s