ugh phosphodiester linkage.\r\n<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fwbjee%252F2014_che_a43.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fwbjee%2F2014_che_a43.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fwbjee%2F2014_che_a43.png?alt=media\">","difficulty":"Easy","source":"WBJEE 2014","_marksId":"64a8140de0ff5a5425a85800"},{"id":117952,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Biomolecules","exam":"Engineering","examName":"WBJEE","q":"Ribose and 2 -deoxyribose can be differentiated by","options":["Fehling's reagent","Tollen's reagent","Barfoed's reagent","Osazone formation"],"answer":3,"solution":"Ribose forms osazone with $\\mathrm{Ph}-\\mathrm{NH}-\\mathrm{NH}_{2}$ whereas in deoxyribose, one - OH group is missing, due to which, it cannot form osazone.\r\n<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fwbjee%252F2013_che_a32.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fwbjee%2F2013_che_a32.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fwbjee%2F2013_che_a32.png?alt=media\">","difficulty":"Medium","source":"WBJEE 2013","_marksId":"64a813f6e0ff5a5425a8572d"},{"id":117953,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Biomolecules","exam":"Engineering","examName":"WBJEE","q":"The correct structure of the dipeptide gly-ala is","options":["<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0